{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaMonoid","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaProd"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_one_sub_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_one_sub_pow","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid.lean#L101-L114","doc":"**The q-analogue of the divisor-free FRT hook product.**\n\n`∏_c (1 − Q^{h_λ(c)}) · ∏_i (β-gaps as 1 − Q^{gap}) = ∏_i ∏_{k=1}^{β_i} (1 − Q^k)`.\n\nNo separate proof: the assembly, like the per-row step, never touched the values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_id","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_mul_betaGapProdF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_mul_betaGapProdF","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid.lean#L78-L95","doc":"**The full divisor-free Frame–Robinson–Thrall hook product, in any commutative monoid.**\n\n`prodHooksF f l · ∏_i betaGapProdF f (l[i]) (l.drop (i+1)) = ∏_i descFactF f (l[i] + |drop|)`.\n\nAt `f = id` over `(ℕ, ×)` this is `SYTBeta.prodHooks_mul_betaGapProd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_eq_prod_rowHookProdF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_eq_prod_rowHookProdF","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid.lean#L67-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_row_eq_rowHookProdF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_row_eq_rowHookProdF","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid.lean#L50-L65","doc":"Row `i` of `prodHooksF` is the per-row `rowHookProdF`.  Same leg simplification as the `ℕ`\nversion — `colLen_eq_succ_add_cnt_drop` is about indices and is reused verbatim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid.lean#L44-L48","doc":"The corpus `prodHooks`, pushed through `f`: `∏_{c ∈ λ} f(h_λ(c))`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}